 gap not triggering), front-end could reprice tightening risk back in quickly."}, {"tag": "policy", "text": "Fed may emphasize sticky core inflation over labor softening, delaying the dovish repricing this trade assumes."}], "trade": {"legs": [{"instrument": "DGS3MO", "weight": 0.4}, {"instrument": "DGS1", "weight": -0.6}], "conviction": 0.45, "rationale": "Labor loosening plus disinflation and easing financial conditions argue for less near-term tightening priced; long the 1y vs 3m captures front-end pricing-out of hikes/pulling forward cuts within 2y limit."}}

{"notes": "Labor: unemployment rate has drifted up from a 3.90 base to 4.20% (12m change +0.30pp), with a rising 3m average (4.13%) and sitting at the top of its 12m range (range_position=1.0). Sahm gap is modestly positive (+0.23pp), not yet recession-triggering but a clear loosening signal. This is a genuine, moderately fresh trend (13 monthly obs, consistent direction over the last few prints) — labor is loosening, which argues for less near-term tightening (dovish).

