 labor softening is already broadly anticipated by market."}], "trade": {"legs": [{"instrument": "DGS6MO", "weight": -0.5}, {"instrument": "DGS2", "weight": -0.5}], "conviction": 0.45, "rationale": "Modest front-end richening (yields lower) reflecting labor-driven reduction in near-term tightening odds, tempered by sticky core inflation; flat weighting across 6mo-2y avoids overcommitting to timing of any cut."}}

{"notes": "Labor: unemployment sits at 4.30 with a 3m decline of -0.10pp but flat 6m and +0.10pp 12m — noisy, range-bound between 4.10-4.50 over the past year, sahm_gap modest at +0.23pp. This reads as a labor market that is neither tightening nor loosening decisively; it's holding roughly steady with a slight recent softening in the last print. Not a clean signal either way — near no-view, tilt very slightly toward loosening given the 3m direction.

